      <title>‘Produce a good result by any means’: how AI is testing South Korea’s exam obsession</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/24/produce-a-good-result-by-any-means-how-ai-is-testing-south-koreas-exam-obsession</link>
      <description>South Korea has made exams a career-defining way to level the playing field, but AI has plunged the system into chaos “I have never worn glasses in my life,” Yun Jeong-hu says to the camera, holding up a tax law textbook, and flipping through pages plastered with notes and dotted with highlighted sections. In the 22-minute video , the 25-year-old talks viewers through his study methods, naming his tutors, describing watching recorded lectures until 3am, and solving a corporate tax question…</description>
